var index = [{"id":"post-50","title":"[in progress] Olive Oil Biscuits","excerpt":" https://www.devglan.com/online-tools/text-encryption-decryption","headings":"","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/in-progress-olive-oil-biscuits.html"},{"id":"post-49","title":"[in progress] Lasagna Roll Ups","excerpt":" https://www.devglan.com/online-tools/text-encryption-decryption","headings":"","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/lasagna-roll-ups.html"},{"id":"post-46","title":"[Sun Oven] Burrito Bowls & Lentil Sloppy Joes for Camping","excerpt":"<p>It was during the pandemic, stuck at home and with an itchy brain, that I was watching some <a href=\"https://cas.appstate.edu/news/cas-continues-zoomer-series-alumni-engagement\">continuing education content from Appalachian State University</a> in my good old home state of North Carolina, and there was an excellent hour-long lecture (<a href=\"https://youtu.be/nUX9nEIOSrU?si=sP81esbf09ZvljbP\">click me to watch</a>) on sustainable cooking using solar. I am <span style=\"text-decoration: line-through;\">cheap</span> <a href=\"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/tags/frugal/\">frugal</a>, I like sustainability, and I like food. This all seemed like a win-win-win, plus I like to camp so this style of cooking could go camping with me and eliminate my low-key resource-anxiety (like range-anxiety, but for propane).</p>\n<p>Through the magic of finding the right influencer for a product I already decided to purchase, I found <a href=\"https://www.sunoven.com/products/stackable-pots-doug-stacy\">some sort of sponsorship deal or special</a> to make owning the All American Sun Oven, which I had settled on, more affordable. It was the pandemic. I was sitting at home anyway. So I bought one.</p>\n<p>But then the question of what to cook came up. A Sun Oven without recipes is just a gadget and not a tool.</p>\n<figure class=\"post__image post__image--center\"><img loading=\"lazy\"  src=\"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/media/posts/46/photo_2025-04-13_11-15-20.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"500\" height=\"667\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1920px) 100vw, 1920px\" srcset=\"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/media/posts/46/responsive/photo_2025-04-13_11-15-20-xs.jpg 640w ,https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/media/posts/46/responsive/photo_2025-04-13_11-15-20-sm.jpg 768w ,https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/media/posts/46/responsive/photo_2025-04-13_11-15-20-md.jpg 1024w ,https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/media/posts/46/responsive/photo_2025-04-13_11-15-20-lg.jpg 1366w ,https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/media/posts/46/responsive/photo_2025-04-13_11-15-20-xl.jpg 1600w ,https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/media/posts/46/responsive/photo_2025-04-13_11-15-20-2xl.jpg 1920w\"></figure>\n<p>It turns out that in addition to being able to bake anything which can bake at lower temperatures in an oven - my Sun Oven never reports being above 300F and for planning purposes should be considered to be 250F, and that's in full sun at the beach - it can also cook any recipes that could otherwise be cooked in a slow cooker/crockpot.</p>\n<p>Bingo.</p>\n","headings":"Table of Contents [Sun Oven] Burrito Bowls Ingredients Materials Method Notes &amp; Bibliography CookLang [Sun Oven] Lentil Sloppy Joes Ingredients Materials Method Notes &amp; Bibliography CookLang Coda","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/sun-oven-burrito-bowls-and-lentil-sloppy-joes.html"},{"id":"post-25","title":"[Instant Pot] Enhanced Boxed Macaroni and Cheese","excerpt":"<p>Happy <a href=\"https://www.neurodiversityweek.com/\">Neurodiversity Celebration Week</a>!</p>\n<figure class=\"post__image post__image--center\" ><img loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\" title=\"https://www.neurodiversityweek.com/\" src=\"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/46eb70_f3849364bd774db99f9ac87b93a6f78d~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_482,h_482,al_c,q_85,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01,enc_avif,quality_auto/We're%20Supporting.png\" alt=\"https://www.neurodiversityweek.com/\" width=\"482\" height=\"482\" data-is-external-image=\"true\">\n<figcaption ><a href=\"https://www.neurodiversityweek.com/\">https://www.neurodiversityweek.com/</a></figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p>There are many types of <a href=\"https://www.neurodiversityweek.com/\">#neurodiversity</a> and <a href=\"https://howtoadhd.com/\">#ADHD</a> is just one of them. A lot of times, an Instant Pot is a godsend for the easily distracted, whether that be adult caregivers to children who have the urge to draw a masterpiece all over the living room in lipstick, or <a href=\"https://www.myaddblog.com/2019/12/instant-pot-best-adhd-tool-of-2019.html\">a person whose brain is the challenge</a>. Which is why so many of my recipes are written for people with executive dysfunction and low working memory, and cover meals that would be faster and, some might find, easier to prepare without the Instant Pot. And today is no exception.</p>\n<p>Today, I present: enhanced boxed macaroni and cheese. It is a mashup of <a href=\"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/instant-pot-fancy-dinner-macaroni-and-cheese.html\">my fancy dinner macaroni and cheese</a> <a href=\"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/tags/frugal/\">frugalized</a> with <a href=\"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/instant-pot-vegetarian-colcannon-2.html\">the boxed macaroni and cheese recipe found elsewhere on this website</a>.</p>\n","headings":"Table of Contents Ingredients. Materials. Method. Notes. Neurodiversity Celebration Week. CookLang.","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/instant-pot-vegetarian-colcannon-3.html"},{"id":"post-42","title":"The Truth About Cooking on a Budget","excerpt":"<p>The internet is wonderful tool for sharing information. It can be especially helpful in finding great budget options for stretching a dollar, especially with food. You found your way here, didn't you?</p>\n<p>But the internet is also a place of fantasy. And a lot of times the budget recipes you might encounter, unless you already have the same <a href=\"#non-existing-page-with-id-36\">capsule kitchen</a> as the influencer, social media personality, blogger, or recipe developer, doesn't always mean a savings over buying that dish from a restaurant. This is why...</p>\n","headings":"","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/the-truth-about-cooking-on-a-budget.html"},{"id":"post-35","title":"[waffle maker] Protein Yogurt Waffles","excerpt":"<p>I make this for breakfast when I am solo-parenting. Kid never rejects it. It is packed with fat, fiber, and protein. And it is made with <a href=\"#non-existing-page-with-id-36\">my personal capsule kitchen's pantry staples</a>.</p>\n","headings":"Table of Contents Ingredients Materials Instructions Notes","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/waffle-maker-protein-yogurt-waffles.html"},{"id":"post-33","title":"[Instant Pot] Gochujangish Buttered Noodles","excerpt":"<p><br>You know what you don't do when living with someone of Chinese extraction? Flaunt how delicious gochujang is. So, don't flaunt it. Just eat it.</p>\n","headings":"Table of Contents Ingredients Materials Method Notes","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/gochujang-buttered-noodles.html"},{"id":"post-32","title":"[Baking] Blueberry Drop Biscuits","excerpt":"<p>Did you know there is a <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/NYTCooking/\">New York Times Cooking subreddit</a>. Oh yes! There is a subreddit for everything. My library provides us with a subscription to the New York Times Cooking section and I generally find most things there to be far more ingredients and steps than my brain could handle, but <a href=\"https://archive.is/kgtcM#selection-2353.0-2357.10\">some absolutely wonderful soul</a> <a href=\"https://redd.it/1ijd6i0\">on the subreddit</a> converted <a href=\"https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1021175-strawberry-drop-biscuits?smid=ck-recipe-iOS-share\">the Strawberry Drop Biscuits recipe by Andrew Purcell</a> into something much more executive dysfunction friendly.</p>\n<p>No rolling. No cutting. One bowl. You can use salted butter - which is what you have on hand, anyway, because it is the best bread butter. And to incorporate the butter it is fun sensory play; plus you don't have to keep the butter cold.</p>\n<p>And they taste like BoBerry Biscuits. Plus they freeze well.</p>\n","headings":"Table of Contents Ingredients Materials Method Notes","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/baking-blueberry-drop-biscuits.html"},{"id":"post-30","title":"[Instant Pot] Mujadara 2.0 - More Dump, Fewer Bowls","excerpt":"<p>I have <a href=\"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/instant-pot-mujadara-vegan.html\">an earlier version of this recipe</a> kicking around and wanted to update now that I've got executive dysfunction AND a toddler. That's double not able to attend to my cooking, so I shifted things around and made this more of a dump-and-go recipe.</p>\n<p>Mujadara is a <a href=\"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/tags/vegan/\">vegan</a>, middle-eastern dish of spiced lentils. It's name means \"pockmarked\" which is in reference to the rice looking pockmarked by the lentils. The spice profile used here is lebanese because yum. In the Notes section, I'll offer other sources of other spice profiles from other countries and cultures.</p>\n","headings":"Table of Contents Ingredients Materials Method Notes","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/instant-pot-mujadara-vegan-2.html"},{"id":"post-23","title":"[Instant Pot] Caramelized Onions","excerpt":"<p>Once, many years ago, I heard a rumor that it was possible to make caramelized onions using a slow cooker. I dutifully followed the directions and ... no. I got <a href=\"#mcetoc_1ii0phsas4eg\">soft, sautéed onions, but not caramelized</a> like I wanted.</p>\n<p>Then came a long series of Reddit rabbit holes which ended up with me checking out <a href=\"https://app.thestorygraph.com/books/8e1619f9-0fc4-4a7b-a1f8-082c30fa6aae\">The Vegan Instant Pot Cookbook</a> from the library (How much do we love our libraries?) and reading the recipe for Caramelized Onion Jam (page 61). Wait a minute, caramelized onions? Hmmm. Can Instant Pot do what the slow cooker couldn't?</p>\n","headings":"Table of Contents Caramelized Onions vs. Sautéed Onions Ingredients Materials Method Notes","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/instant-pot-caramelized-onions.html"},{"id":"post-1","title":"[Instant Pot] Fancy Dinner Macaroni and Cheese","excerpt":"<p>When The Mister and I were courting, we weren't well off enough to afford restaurant dates. So, we would have \"Fancy Dinner\" which is where we cooked something we would otherwise purchase at a restaurant, but for below-restaurant prices at home. This macaroni and cheese recipe qualifies. It is more expensive to make than <a href=\"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/instant-pot-vegetarian-colcannon-2.html\">a sub-$1 box of store brand</a>, however every extra penny is worth it in the taste department.</p>\n","headings":"Table of Contents Ingredients. Materials. Instructions. Notes.","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/instant-pot-fancy-dinner-macaroni-and-cheese.html"},{"id":"post-27","title":"Taco Seasoning","excerpt":"<p>I love a good make-ahead spice mix. It helps in terms of economizing if you can make it in a large enough batch and/or have multiple people to part it out between. Much as we did with the <a href=\"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/mccormicks-butter-chicken-spice-mix.html\">makhani spice mix</a>, here's the recipe to replicate a packet of taco seasoning.</p>\n","headings":"Ingredients for the Spice Mix Materials Method","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/taco-seasoning-mix.html"},{"id":"post-28","title":"Brown Sugar from Pantry Staples","excerpt":"<p>If you have been hanging out, snooping <a href=\"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes\">my recipe book</a> for a while, you know that I am all about <a href=\"#non-existing-page-with-id-36\">that capsule kitchen</a>, which means that certain items which are pantry staples for others, are just an additional bit of recipe for me. Such as brown sugar.</p>\n","headings":"","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/brown-sugar.html"},{"id":"post-44","title":"[baking] Minimal Effort Peach Pie","excerpt":"<p>Today is <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pi_Day\">Pi Day</a>! While I much prefer to buy my pies and let some food processing robotic line somewhere handle pie crust and keeping the edges unburnt while getting the middle cooked through, when someone has dietary restrictions that don't allow for robot pie baking lines to labor for me, it means I have to cook it myself. Ughhhhhhh.</p>\n<p>Here's a recipe that never lets me down. Crumble topping so I don't have to deal with that most finicky of pie crust edge burning annoyances.</p>\n<p>See the notes section at the end of this recipe for the simple substitutions one needs to make this vegan.</p>\n","headings":"Table of Contents Ingredients Materials Instructions Notes","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/baking-minimal-effort-peach-pie.html"},{"id":"post-3","title":"[Instant Pot] Vegetarian Japanese Golden Curry","excerpt":"<p>Have you had Golden Curry? It is the tongue-satisfying corporeal embodiment of the flavor: umami. It is stew, cooked in a fraction of the time it takes to cook stew. And it can be cooked entirely in the Instant Pot.</p>\n<p>I know there are other Instant Pot Japanese Golden Curry recipes, but they all contain meat and use pressure. This one is just the sauté feature and is <a href=\"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/tags/vegetarian/\">vegetarian</a>, making it a dish that can be cooked anywhere there is a power outlet.</p>\n<p>Golden curry is WORK though. Nothing minimal effort here. Lots of stirring and cutting on the front end. On the back end is a lot of waiting. This is probably why people in Japan only have this dish a few times a month.</p>\n","headings":"Table of Contents Ingredients Materials Instructions Notes","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/instant-pot-vegetarian-japanese-golden-curry-2.html"},{"id":"post-5","title":"[Instant Pot] Close Enough to Eggplant Parm (on Pasta)","excerpt":"<p>I was craving <em>Eggplant Parmesan </em>(aka <em>Eggplant Parmigiano</em>), but I really, really hate making it myself. There's the slicing of the eggplant, the salting of the eggplant, the dabbing away of eggplant moisture, the breading of the eggplant, and I could go on forever.</p>\n<p>So I usually buy this one. All the better to let someone else do the labors and me enjoy the flavors. My favorite <em>Eggplant Parm</em> dealer, <a href=\"http://www.alfredospizzavillachapelhill.com/\">Alfredo's Pizza Villa</a>, has an option to serve it over pasta.</p>\n<p>Could I recreate that at home? In the Instant Pot?</p>\n<p>The answer is, \"No.\" But I can come very close.</p>\n","headings":"Table of Contents Ingredients Materials Instructions Notes","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/instant-pot-close-enough-to-eggplant-parm-on-pasta.html"},{"id":"post-4","title":"Lemon Fruit Yogurt Cake","excerpt":"<p>Do you have fruit that is about to go bad? This recipe will help you turn it into a muffin-cake type thing in no time. It is <a href=\"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/tags/vegetarian/\">#vegetarian</a>, but not vegan, on account of the eggs and yogurt; I have not tested this with dairy-free yogurt nor a functional egg substitute. I have tested <a href=\"https://heartofabaker.com/vegan-baking-basics-cornstarch-water-egg-substitute/\">the cornstarch-and-water egg substitute</a> and the cake doesn't work well, but no egg substitutes beyond that. If you test dairy-free yogurt or find an egg substitute that works, give me a comment to let me know how it fares.</p>\n<p>This cake works quite nicely as a sheet birthday cake (<a href=\"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/tags/birthdaycake/\">#birthdaycake</a>), without the need to ice, as the fruit topping adds that extra delight that icing typically does. Tested at a 9 year old's birthday party to the happy smiles of all and the delight of parents that it only contains 1/2 cup of added sugar for the whole cake.</p>\n","headings":"Table of Contents INGREDIENTS and MATERIALS Wets Dries Toppings Materials PREPWORK INSTRUCTIONS NOTES","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/lemon-fruit-yogurt-cake.html"},{"id":"post-18","title":"McCormick's Butter Chicken Spice Mix","excerpt":"<div id=\"wrapper\"><header>\n<div id=\"header\" class=\"container\">\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"component container\">\n<div class=\"component-content\">\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"component row-splitter\">\n<div class=\" header-desktop-view container-fluid\">\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"row component column-splitter\">\n<div class=\"col-6 col-sm-4 col-md-3 col-lg-2\">\n<div class=\"row\">\n<div class=\"component image site-logo gggg col-12\">\n<div class=\"component-content\">A long, long time ago in a galaxy right where you are currently located, there was a lovely company called</div>\n<div class=\"component-content\"><a title=\"Logo\" href=\"https://www.mccormick.com/\"><figure class=\"post__image post__image--center\"><img loading=\"lazy\"  src=\"https://www.mccormick.com/-/media/project/oneweb/mccormick-us/global/site-logos/mccormick-logo.png?h=120&amp;iar=0&amp;w=120&amp;rev=051aba0ec6ab4ce1901dcccb6eade2ef&amp;hash=CB4C1B21DE0F0F71A65663F5A753C503\" alt=\"mccormick-logo\" width=\"120\" height=\"120\" data-variantitemid=\"{8818F85F-4209-46B6-A5AC-7EFC1A61AC5C}\" data-variantfieldname=\"Image\" data-is-external-image=\"true\"></figure></a></div>\n<div class=\"component-content\">which produced the very best Makhani spice packet that could ever be purchased at a standard American grocery store. It was so good, in fact, that when they discontinued the spice packet, people took to the internet to seek a duplicate. There were none to be found.</div>\n<div> </div>\n<div>SEVEN years later, McCormick finally has posted the recipe on their website. In fear that the page on their website will disappear at some point, like the spice blend did, it is being archived <a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20240720151755/https://www.mccormick.com/recipes/main-dishes/butter-chicken\">here</a>, <a href=\"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/media/files/Butter Chicken _ McCormick.pdf\">here</a>, <a href=\"https://archive.is/KNk1P\">here</a>, and here on this blog for posterity. We must not lose this flavor again!</div>\n<div>","headings":"Butter Chicken Will this recipe give the same results as using the packet that has been discontinued? I really love the flavors that were in that. It would be great if you brought it back.","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/mccormicks-butter-chicken-spice-mix.html"},{"id":"post-8","title":"[Instant Pot] Boxed Macaroni and Cheese","excerpt":"<p> </p>\n<p>Happy <a href=\"https://www.neurodiversityweek.com/\">Neurodiversity Week</a>!</p>\n<figure class=\"aentry-post__figure aentry-post__figure--text-width aentry-post__figure--has-text\" data-figure-type=\"image\" data-image-type=\"standart\">\n<div class=\"aentry-post__img--text-width\">\n<div class=\"aentry-post__img--text-width\"><img loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\" title=\"https://www.neurodiversityweek.com/\" src=\"https://ic.pics.livejournal.com/theinfamousj/101655/42664/42664_original.png\" alt=\"https://www.neurodiversityweek.com/\" data-is-external-image=\"true\"></div>\n</div>\n<figcaption><a href=\"https://www.neurodiversityweek.com/\">https://www.neurodiversityweek.com/</a></figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p>There are many types of #neurodiversity and #ADHD is just one of them. A lot of times, an Instant Pot is a godsend for the easily distracted, whether that be adult caregivers to children who have the urge to draw a masterpiece all over the living room in lipstick, or <a href=\"https://www.myaddblog.com/2019/12/instant-pot-best-adhd-tool-of-2019.html\">a person whose brain is the child trying to draw a masterpiece all over the neural-living room with cognitive-lipstick</a>. Which is why so many of my recipes are written for people with low working memory and cover meals that would be faster and, some might find, easier to prepare without the Instant Pot. And today is no exception. Today, I present: boxed macaroni and cheese.</p>\n","headings":"Materials. Method. NOTES","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/instant-pot-vegetarian-colcannon-2.html"},{"id":"post-7","title":"[Instant Pot] Vegetarian Colcannon","excerpt":"<p class=\"msg msg--success\"><em>Have you ever had colcannon? A St. Patrick's day favorite, colcannon is an Irish potato recipe.</em> [<a href=\"https://www.simplyrecipes.com/recipes/colcannon/#:~:text=Have%20you%20ever%20had%20colcannon%3F%20A%20St.%20Patrick%27s%20day%20favorite%2C%20colcannon%20is%20an%20Irish%20potato%20recipe%2C%20a%20mixture%20of%20creamy%20mashed%20potatoes%20and%20usually%20kale%20or%20cabbage.\">source</a>] <em>At its most essential, the colcannon recipe is mashed potatoes mixed with chopped cabbage or kale. Other additions like bacon, ham, scallions or yellow onions are also common.</em> [<a href=\"https://barefeetinthekitchen.com/irish-colcannon-potatoes-with-bacon-and-cabbage-recipe/#:~:text=At%20its%20most%20essential%2C%20the%20colcannon%20recipe%20is%20mashed%20potatoes%20mixed%20with%20chopped%20cabbage%20or%20kale.%20Other%20additions%20like%20bacon%2C%20ham%2C%20scallions%20or%20yellow%20onions%20are%20also%20common.\">source</a>]</p>\n<p>Happy St. Patrick's Day. I'm not Christian, but <a href=\"https://www.mashed.com/738103/the-untold-truth-of-corned-beef/#:~:text=Corned%20beef%20might%20have%20some%20Jewish%20influence\">due to the influence that my religion has had on St. Patrick's Day</a>, I like to celebrate it in all of its green and delicious mealed glory. And now so can you!</p>\n","headings":"Table of Contents Ingredients Materials Method <strong>Serving suggestions</strong>","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/instant-pot-vegetarian-colcannon.html"},{"id":"post-9","title":"Vegetarian Orange \"Chicken\"","excerpt":"<p>Since we still haven't yet had <a href=\"https://www.joincake.com/blog/chinese-lantern-festival/\">the Lantern Festival</a>, I've been craving the tastes of China and Taiwan which my partner cooks always (it is his food culture) but tonight is my night to cook and I know this is a totally Americanized dish, but <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/2021/11/22/1058132899/ask-code-switch-thought-for-food\">I've been listening to Code Switch and they claim that it is completely authentic to adapt to new flavors from a Chinese lens</a>, so I'm going with it.</p>\n","headings":"Materials. Method. <strong>NOTES</strong>","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/vegetarian-orange-chicken.html"},{"id":"post-17","title":"[Instant Pot] Vegetarian Lasagna Soup","excerpt":"<p>Craving a lasagna but don't have access to an oven? This soup'll do ya! This recipe can be cooked in a crock pot/slow cooker instead of an Instant Pot if you cook the included lentils a different way. This recipe can be made vegan if you substitute vegan cheese for cow cheese.</p>\n","headings":"INGREDIENTS INSTRUCTIONS NOTES","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/instant-pot-vegetarian-lasagna-soup.html"},{"id":"post-16","title":"[Dehydrator] Citrus Zest","excerpt":"<p>IN SEASON ALERT! It is winter and that means citrus is in season so that means they are cheap and plentiful!</p>\n<p>As a person with executive dysfunction, I loathe grating citrus zest. One of the substitutes I like to make is a powdered citrus peel. I make this from the peel of citrus fruits I was otherwise eating anyway, and simply reserve the peel for this extra process. This is a <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/noscrapleftbehind\">/r/NoScrapLeftBehind</a> kind of <a href=\"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/tags/frugal/\">#frugal</a> winner.</p>\n<p>It is very simple to make: raw (as in not boiled to otherwise cooked) citrus peel (including pith) dehydrated and then ground up in a spice grinder.</p>\n<figure class=\"aentry-post__figure aentry-post__figure--vertical-mobile aentry-post__figure--has-text\" data-figure-type=\"image\" data-image-type=\"verticalMobile\">\n<div class=\"aentry-post__img--vertical-mobile\">\n<div class=\"aentry-post__img--vertical-mobile\"><figure class=\"post__image post__image--center\"><img loading=\"lazy\"  style=\"max-width: 100%;\" title=\"4 oz of citrus peel, including pith, weighed in a coffee filter on my messy kitchen table\" src=\"https://ic.pics.livejournal.com/theinfamousj/101655/41170/41170_540.jpg\" sizes=\"500px\" srcset=\"https://ic.pics.livejournal.com/theinfamousj/101655/41170/41170_540.jpg 540w, https://ic.pics.livejournal.com/theinfamousj/101655/41170/41170_1000.jpg 1000w\" alt=\"4 oz of citrus peel, including pith, weighed in a coffee filter on my messy kitchen table\" width=\"500\" height=\"281\" data-inherit-privacy=\"true\" data-is-external-image=\"true\"></figure></div>\n</div>\n<figcaption>4 oz of citrus peel, including pith, weighed in a coffee filter on my messy kitchen table</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<p>Want that in more detail?</p>\n","headings":"Table of Contents <strong>Materials List</strong> <strong>Procedure</strong> Notes","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/dehydrator-citrus-zest.html"},{"id":"post-19","title":"[Instant Pot] Apple Core Jam","excerpt":"<p>Let there be <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/noscrapleftbehind/\">/r/NoScrapLeftBehind</a> with this way to render apple cores and peels into usable jam. Cook it in the Instant Pot for easy cleanup and a generally hands-off experience. And to make it even more <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/noscrapleftbehind/\">NoScrapLeftBehind</a>, try cleaning your Instant Pot's inner pot with just water as a first rinse to get some jam-juice to drink.</p>\n<figure class=\"aentry-post__figure aentry-post__figure--media\">\n<div class=\"fb-post\" data-href=\"https://www.facebook.com/NannyJenL/posts/3857094657693400\" data-width=\"500\">\n<div class=\"fb-xfbml-parse-ignore\"><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/NannyJenL/posts/3857094657693400\">Facebook post</a></div>\n<div>","headings":"Materials List: Procedure: NOTES","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/instant-pot-apple-core-jam.html"},{"id":"post-20","title":"[Microwave] Egg and Cheese Sandwich","excerpt":"<p>Why would you cook an egg in a microwave? Because children sense when you are involved in a time-sensitive task that requires your concentration and attention and seize the opportunity. But with a microwave, you're not (involved in a time-sensitive task that requires your concentration and attention) and all you sacrifice is that small bit of flavor from the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rs1JLYXROVU\">Maillard reaction</a> you're also not engaging in. Your move, children!</p>\n","headings":"Materials List: Procedure: NOTES","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/microwave-egg-and-cheese-sandwich.html"},{"id":"post-15","title":"[Dehydrator] MYO Beet Root Powder","excerpt":"<p>IN SEASON ALERT! It is the beginning of April and the ingredients you'll need are in season so that means they are cheap and plentiful!</p>\n","headings":"Materials List Procedure NOTES","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/myo-beet-root-powder.html"},{"id":"post-14","title":"Unsweet Dry Bean Soymilk in the Joyoung DJ13U-P10 Soymilk Maker","excerpt":"<figure class=\"post__image post__image--left\"><img loading=\"lazy\"  style=\"max-width: 100%;\" src=\"https://ic.pics.livejournal.com/theinfamousj/101655/35959/35959_original.jpg\" width=\"30%\" data-is-external-image=\"true\"></figure>\n<p>This is a very specific recipe for a very specific machine which I happen to have access to. The instructions which come with it do contain an English potion which has recipes for whole soy beans but say \"wet and dry beans\".</p>\n<p>Wet beans means that you've thought about it ahead of time and soaked your soy beans. Those of you who have been a reader of my blog for a while know that I'm not that person. And I don't want to pull out my Instant Pot in order to quick-soak the soy beans, either.</p>\n<p>So I figured out a recipe to make soy milk in this maker from 100% dry beans!</p>\n<p>Let's get to it!</p>\n","headings":"Ingredients Procedure NOTES","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/unsweet-dry-bean-soymilk-in-the-joyoung-dj13u-p10-soymilk-maker.html"},{"id":"post-13","title":"[Instant Pot] Frozen Cheese Tortellini from Wegmans","excerpt":"<p>I can never, ever get tortellini right on the stove top. It either is too gummy or not fully cooked. But with an Instant Pot, it is perfect, every time. And you can too!</p>\n<p>As for any other frozen tortellini brands, it will work identically. Don't try this with refrigerated tortellini as it is too delicate. <a href=\"https://marginmakingmom.com/instant-pot-tortellini/#:~:text=HOW%20TO%20COOK%20DRIED%20TORTELLINI%20IN%20THE%20INSTANT%20POT\">Dry tortellini has its own recipe</a>.</p>\n<p>I also want to say that this doesn't include sauce. You are on your own to figure out sauce (like, say, from a jar or can), or use a recipe that cooks the sauce and the tortellini together all yummy-like.</p>\n<p>This recipe just gets you from frozen plain cheese-tortellini to cooked plain cheese-tortellini.</p>\n<p>Use case: Children who cannot agree on a sauce and you'd like to automate the tortellini cooking process so that you can spend more time with them.</p>\n","headings":"Ingredients/Materials Procedure","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/instant-pot-frozen-cheese-tortellini-from-wegmans.html"},{"id":"post-12","title":"[Instant Pot] Defrost a Frozen Bagel","excerpt":"<p>There are many ways to defrost frozen bagels and using your Instant Pot to do it seems very cumbersome. But me being me, I've been in a situation where I had my Instant Pot to cook with and nothing else, namely: travel.</p>\n<p>You see, when I cannot arrange a HospEx homestay through CouchSurfing or BeWelcome, I'll stay in a hotel that might or might not have a microwave. So I always bring my Instant Pot. I also bring an extremely good cooler with dry ice in so that I can keep frozen foods frozen, and bagels as well as some of my <a href=\"https://theinfamousj.livejournal.com/505482.html\">earlier mentioned portioned meals</a> are usually enjoying the dry-ice chill.</p>\n<p>So aside from taking a bagel out and leaving it on the counter overnight (which you know I don't do because I'm not one for thinking ahead), I figured out how to do it perfectly in an Instant Pot.</p>\n","headings":"Ingredients/Materials Procedure NOTES","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/instant-pot-defrost-a-frozen-bagel.html"},{"id":"post-11","title":"[Instant Pot] Mujadara *vegan*","excerpt":"<p>This is a <a href=\"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/tags/vegan/\">vegan</a> Lebanese dish of spiced lentils, though Egypt has a similar dish (different spice profile, natch). If you have <strong>lentils</strong>, <strong>onion</strong>, <strong>garlic</strong>, <strong>rice</strong>, and some olive (or other high temp) <strong>oil</strong> kicking around and you want a quick and filling meal, this is a good dish to try.</p>\n<p>You will need two mixing bowls, a knife, a big stirring spoon, and a cutting board as well as the Instant Pot. Also, if you want, a third mixing bowl and a strainer that fits within it so that you can freeze up some vegetable stock.</p>\n","headings":"Table of Contents Ingredients First things First: The Prep-work Second things Second: Sautéing Third things Third: The Lid Goes On Fourth things Fourth: Serving Notes","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/instant-pot-mujadara-vegan.html"},{"id":"post-10","title":"[Instant Pot] Wegmans Italian Classics Cheese Tortellini","excerpt":"<p>Why would anyone write Instant Pot instructions for a frozen skillet meal? Small children taking every opportunity to try to destroy the house while you are slaving over a hot stove you cannot step away from, that's why!</p>\n<p>I have not tested this recipe with any other frozen skillet meal but the one listed in the title, yet I highly suspect that it will work identically. If you try it, <a href=\"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/authors/j/\">drop me a line</a> and let me know whether my suspicions are accurate.</p>\n","headings":"Ingredients/Materials Procedure Notes","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/instant-pot-wegmans-italian-classics-cheese-tortellini.html"},{"id":"post-22","title":"[Instant Pot] Vegan Vegetable Soup","excerpt":"<p>Let's talk about <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/noscrapleftbehind/\">No Scrap Left Behind</a>, which is one of my frequented subreddits. It is a movement all about taking the scraps from one recipe and using them in a different recipe. Since I'm a vegetarian, my scraps are almost always vegetables. And so, I make soup. In my Instant Pot. And so can you!</p>\n","headings":"Ingredients First Things First: The Sautéing Second Things Second: Everything Else Third Things Third: The Optional Step Last Things Last: Eat","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/instant-pot-vegan-vegetable-soup.html"},{"id":"post-34","title":"[Instant Pot] Vegan Cincinnati Chili | Total Time Required 1 hr 10 mins","excerpt":"<p>First, let me say that this recipe is not a quick way to put dinner on the table, but in terms of actual time you have to do any actual thing, it will only involve your human labor for about 10 minutes. Meets my patient-yet-lazy standards.</p>\n","headings":"Table of Contents Ingredients/Shopping List Materials Method the Pasta Method the Cincinnati Chili","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/instant-pot-vegan-cincinnati-chili-or-total-time-required-1-hr-10-mins.html"},{"id":"post-40","title":"[dehydrator] How To Store Extra Onion | Not Quick; Total Time Days","excerpt":"<p>Don't you hate recipes that call for 1/2 an onion or 1/4 an onion? I do. What am I going to do with the rest of the onion? I do batch cooking, so it will be a long time before I get to using up the rest of that onion. I used to just throw the whole onion in, but that often times would upset the flavor balance.<br><br>But then I figured it out: dehydrate the onion.<br><br>Need that in more detail?</p>\n","headings":"Tools to Make This Easier","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/how-to-store-extra-onion-or-not-quick-total-time-days.html"},{"id":"post-31","title":"[Instant Pot] Vegetarian Chili Mac & Cheese | Not Quick; Total Time 6 hours","excerpt":"<p>First, let me say that this recipe is not a quick way to put dinner on the table, but in terms of actual time you have to do any actual thing, it will only involve your human labor for about 15 minutes. Meets my patient-yet-lazy standards!</p>\n","headings":"Table of Contents Ingredients Materials First Things First: The Beans Second Things Second: The Lentils Third Things Third: Low Pressure Slow Cooking of all the Things Fourth Things Fourth: Mac and Cheese Fifth Things Fifth: Mac WITH Cheese Notes Update","author":"J","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/instant-pot-vegetarian-chili-mac-and-cheese-or-not-quick-total-time-6-hours.html"},{"id":"page-21","title":"Tools To Make Executive Dysfunction Cooking Easier","excerpt":"Apron (dishwasherable) Danish Dough Whisk Dehydrator Dishwasher Exam Gloves Flat Stirring thing for Instant Pot Food Freezing Molds - 2 cup, 2 TBSP Food Processor Food Scale Garlic Press Hinged Chopper / Onion Dicer Immersion Blender Instant Pot Mason Jar Vacuum (for storing dry goods&hellip;","headings":"","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/tools-to-make-executive-dysfunction-cooking-easier.html"},{"id":"page-24","title":"Instant Pot Glossary","excerpt":"Term Definition Learn More Link Natural Release Natural Release (NR or NPR) means to let pressure inside Instant Pot to come down on its own. Leave it alone. Do nothing. https://ifoodreal.com/how-to-natural-release-instant-pot/ Quick Release Open the sealed vent and let all the steam out. https://ifoodreal.com/how-to-quick-release-instant-pot/ High&hellip;","headings":"<strong>Term</strong> <strong>Definition</strong> <strong>Learn More Link</strong>","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/instant-pot-glossary.html"},{"id":"page-26","title":"Kitchen Techniques to Make Hard Things Easier","excerpt":"Sometimes, we do things the hard way because no one ever showed us the easy way to do them. Here are some videos taken from all over the internet with a variety of cooking-related techniques explained in a way that will make the hard stuff&hellip;","headings":"Table of Contents Maintaining Kitchen Equipment Sharpening Knife Keeping Knife Sharp Cutting Things Cut Onions into Rainbows Peel Garlic Wicked Fast Mash Garlic with Just a Knife, Cutting Board, and Salt Ran-giri Cut of Carrots Preserving Things Nonstick All the Things Stainless Steel (Inner Pot) is Already Nonstick Butter Wrapper Nonstick Trick Glazing Things","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/kitchen-techniques-to-make-hard-things-easier.html"},{"id":"page-36","title":"Capsule Kitchen Pantry Staples","excerpt":"Fresh Produce Garlic Onion Lemon Nonperishable / Dry all purpose flour baking soda white sugar dry whole milk chickpea flour (to substitute as egg) citrus zest kosher salt vanilla protein powder vegetable bullion lentils dried chickpeas white rice long spaghetti-like dried pasta more chunky noodle&hellip;","headings":"Fresh Produce Nonperishable / Dry Sauces Fats &amp; Oils Spices Non-Food Consumables","metaDescription":"","config":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/capsule-kitchen-pantry-staples.html"},{"id":"tag-1","title":"vegetarian","excerpt":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/tags/vegetarian/"},{"id":"tag-2","title":"instant pot","excerpt":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/tags/instant-pot/"},{"id":"tag-3","title":"fancy dinner","excerpt":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/tags/fancy-dinner/"},{"id":"tag-4","title":"dairy","excerpt":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/tags/dairy/"},{"id":"tag-5","title":"mac & cheese","excerpt":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/tags/mac-and-cheese/"},{"id":"tag-6","title":"birthdaycake","excerpt":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/tags/birthdaycake/"},{"id":"tag-7","title":"dessert","excerpt":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/tags/dessert/"},{"id":"tag-8","title":"frugal","excerpt":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/tags/frugal/"},{"id":"tag-9","title":"vegan","excerpt":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/tags/vegan/"},{"id":"tag-10","title":"ingredient or component","excerpt":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/tags/ingredient-or-component/"},{"id":"tag-11","title":"slow cooker / crockpot","excerpt":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/tags/slow-cooker-crockpot/"},{"id":"tag-12","title":"baking","excerpt":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/tags/baking/"},{"id":"tag-13","title":"sun oven","excerpt":"The All American Sun Oven is a solar cooker which can cook anything an oven can cook as well as anything a crockpot can cook, using just the power of the sun. So long as there is enough sunlight to cast a shadow, cooking can take place. Not cheap, but great for off grid living or off grid camping.\nhttps://www.sunoven.com/collections/shop-sun-oven/products/sun-oven-doug-and-stacy-edition\nGo Sun, a competitor, also offers a commercially available solar cooker. I own the Go Sun Go. Recipes for that specific cooker will also find their way under this tag.\nhttps://gosun.co/products/gosunpro-portable-solar-oven","metaDescription":"","url":"https://theinfamousj.github.io/ExecutiveDysfunctionRecipes/tags/sun-oven/"}];window.publiiStaticSearchInitCallback(index);